[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2544031617","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100447#issuecomment-2544031617","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100447","id":2544031617,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6XoteB","user":{"login":"darksylinc","id":3395130,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTUxMzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3395130?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc","html_url":"https://github.com/darksylinc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-15T19:58:26Z","updated_at":"2024-12-15T19:58:26Z","body":"The function `ResourceFormatSaver::save` performs a GDVIRTUAL_CALL():\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nError ResourceFormatSaver::save(const Ref<Resource> &p_resource, const String &p_path, uint32_t p_flags, const int p_integrity_level) {\r\n\tError err = ERR_METHOD_NOT_FOUND;\r\n\tGDVIRTUAL_CALL(_save, p_resource, p_path, p_flags, p_integrity_level, err);\r\n\treturn err;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI don't know if this breaks the GD ABI and if so, how to implement a fallback function.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2544031617/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2545064001","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100447#issuecomment-2545064001","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100447","id":2545064001,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6XsphB","user":{"login":"RandomShaper","id":11797174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3MTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11797174?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper","html_url":"https://github.com/RandomShaper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-16T09:35:17Z","updated_at":"2024-12-16T09:35:17Z","body":"It may be better to fuse the integrity flags with the mode flags to preserve compatibility.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2545064001/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2545746851","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100447#issuecomment-2545746851","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100447","id":2545746851,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6XvQOj","user":{"login":"darksylinc","id":3395130,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTUxMzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3395130?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc","html_url":"https://github.com/darksylinc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-16T14:16:58Z","updated_at":"2024-12-16T14:16:58Z","body":"> It may be better to fuse the integrity flags with the mode flags to preserve compatibility.\r\n\r\nAhhh!!!! That's a lot more KISS. I like it. Way less effort and more backwards compatible. I'll incorporate that change.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2545746851/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2545817263","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100447#issuecomment-2545817263","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100447","id":2545817263,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Xvhav","user":{"login":"darksylinc","id":3395130,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTUxMzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3395130?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc","html_url":"https://github.com/darksylinc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-16T14:45:05Z","updated_at":"2024-12-16T14:45:05Z","body":"> Ahhh!!!! That's a lot more KISS. I like it. Way less effort and more backwards compatible. I'll incorporate that change.\r\n\r\nArgh!\r\n\r\nI spoke too soon.\r\n\r\nThe main problem is `ResourceFormatSaver::save` and similar virtual functions. But unfortunately they do not include access flags (nor they should). The value of making integrity levels part of access types is a lot less appealing now.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2545817263/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2545853556","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100447#issuecomment-2545853556","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100447","id":2545853556,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6XvqR0","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-16T14:59:02Z","updated_at":"2024-12-16T14:59:02Z","body":"> It may be better to fuse the integrity flags with the mode flags to preserve compatibility.\r\n\r\nNot sure if it's better compatibility:\r\n- custom `FileAccess` implementations might use (internal do exactly this) `(mode_flags == WRITE)` or similar checks.\r\n- `ModeFlags` name imply that it is i/o mode of operation not generic flags, and it is defined as `Enum`, not `BitField` (renaming it and changing type is more breaking than adding new argument).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2545853556/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2545867835","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100447#issuecomment-2545867835","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100447","id":2545867835,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Xvtw7","user":{"login":"darksylinc","id":3395130,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTUxMzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3395130?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc","html_url":"https://github.com/darksylinc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-16T15:04:28Z","updated_at":"2024-12-16T15:04:28Z","body":"> > It may be better to fuse the integrity flags with the mode flags to preserve compatibility.\r\n> \r\n> Not sure if it's better compatibility:\r\n> \r\n>     * custom `FileAccess` implementations might use (internal do exactly this) `(mode_flags == WRITE)` or similar checks.\r\n> \r\n>     * `ModeFlags` name imply that it is i/o mode of operation not generic flags, and it is defined as `Enum`, not `BitField` (renaming it and changing type is more breaking than adding new argument).\r\n\r\nGotcha. Yeah, I think I prefer the current solution of using a separate enum.\r\n\r\nSlightly unrelated to that, I think I prefer that, instead of modifying `ResourceSaver::save` to add `p_integrity_level` to each function overload, to modify SaverFlags:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nenum SaverFlags {\r\n\t\tFLAG_NONE = 0,\r\n\t\tFLAG_RELATIVE_PATHS = 1,\r\n\t\tFLAG_BUNDLE_RESOURCES = 2,\r\n\t\tFLAG_CHANGE_PATH = 4,\r\n\t\tFLAG_OMIT_EDITOR_PROPERTIES = 8,\r\n\t\tFLAG_SAVE_BIG_ENDIAN = 16,\r\n\t\tFLAG_COMPRESS = 32,\r\n\t\tFLAG_REPLACE_SUBRESOURCE_PATHS = 64,\r\n\t\tFLAG_SAVE_INTEGRITY_NONE = 128, // New flag!\r\n\t\tFLAG_SAVE_INTEGRITY_SAVE_SWAP = 256, // New flag!\r\n\t\tFLAG_SAVE_INTEGRITY_SAVE_SWAP_PLUS_SYNC = FLAG_SAVE_INTEGRITY_NONE | FLAG_SAVE_INTEGRITY_SAVE_SWAP, // New flag!\r\n\t};\r\n```\r\n\r\nNot setting any flag will use `SAVE_INTEGRITY_DEFAULT`. Else you can explicitly specify what save integrity you want. And this is a lot more backwards compatible.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2545867835/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2545904031","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100447#issuecomment-2545904031","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100447","id":2545904031,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Xv2mf","user":{"login":"RandomShaper","id":11797174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3MTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11797174?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper","html_url":"https://github.com/RandomShaper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-16T15:17:55Z","updated_at":"2024-12-16T15:17:55Z","body":"As much as I'm a fan of trying to overload the current enums, that looks too awkward:\r\n`swap + sync = none + swap`","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2545904031/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2549509535","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100447#issuecomment-2549509535","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100447","id":2549509535,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6X9m2f","user":{"login":"darksylinc","id":3395130,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTUxMzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3395130?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc","html_url":"https://github.com/darksylinc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-17T20:08:51Z","updated_at":"2024-12-17T20:18:17Z","body":"I've got a question.\r\n\r\nThere is this [validation error](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/actions/runs/12380528008/job/34557165381?pr=100447):\r\n\r\n```\r\nValidate extension JSON: Error: Field 'classes/ResourceFormatSaver/methods/_save/arguments': size changed value in new API, from 3 to 4.\r\n```\r\n\r\nThat belongs to a GDVIRTUAL:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nclass ResourceFormatSaver : public RefCounted {\r\n\t// BEFORE:\r\n\tGDVIRTUAL3R(Error, _save, Ref<Resource>, String, uint32_t)\r\n\t// AFTER:\r\n\tGDVIRTUAL4R(Error, _save, Ref<Resource>, String, uint32_t, int)\r\n};\r\n\r\nError ResourceFormatSaver::save(const Ref<Resource> &p_resource, const String &p_path, uint32_t p_flags, int p_integrity_level) {\r\n\tError err = ERR_METHOD_NOT_FOUND;\r\n\t// BEFORE:\r\n\tGDVIRTUAL_CALL(_save, p_resource, p_path, p_flags, err);\r\n\t// AFTER:\r\n\tGDVIRTUAL_CALL(_save, p_resource, p_path, p_flags, p_integrity_level, err);\r\n\treturn err;\r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid ResourceFormatSaver::_bind_methods() {\r\n\t// BEFORE:\r\n\tGDVIRTUAL_BIND(_save, \"resource\", \"path\", \"flags\");\r\n\t// AFTER:\r\n\tGDVIRTUAL_BIND(_save, \"resource\", \"path\", \"flags\", \"integrity_level\");\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nIs there a way to deal with this in a backwards compatible way? Or do we just drop the integrity_level argument?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2549509535/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2549709332","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100447#issuecomment-2549709332","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100447","id":2549709332,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6X-XoU","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-17T21:48:19Z","updated_at":"2024-12-17T21:48:41Z","body":"> Is there a way to deal with this in a backwards compatible way?\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, there isn't a way to change the signature of virtual methods in a backwards compatible way.\r\n\r\nOne option is adding a new virtual method with the new signature, and then using `GDVIRTUAL_IS_OVERRIDDEN()` to call the new one if implemented, and then fall back on the old one if it isn't implemented?\r\n\r\nI don't think we've actually done that anywhere yet - so far, I think we've always found some other way to work around it, so I don't have any examples to point to. However, we have a similar issue with GDExtension interface functions, and there we have the convention of adding an incrementing integer to each new version of the function. Not the most attractive API, but it works...","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2549709332/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2552120795","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100447#issuecomment-2552120795","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100447","id":2552120795,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YHkXb","user":{"login":"darksylinc","id":3395130,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTUxMzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3395130?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc","html_url":"https://github.com/darksylinc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-18T19:35:20Z","updated_at":"2024-12-18T19:35:20Z","body":"All checks passed. All questions cleared. This PR is ready for review.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2552120795/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2896161230","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100447#issuecomment-2896161230","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100447","id":2896161230,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sn-nO","user":{"login":"darksylinc","id":3395130,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTUxMzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3395130?v=4","gravatar_id